          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 55-year-old man of Black African ancestry is diagnosed with uncomplicated stag</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 55-year-old man of Black African ancestry is diagnosed with uncomplicated stage 1 hypertension. He has no diabetes, kidney disease, or heart failure. Which of the following is the MOST appropriate initial monotherapy?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ramipril</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>ACE inhibitors are less effective as monotherapy in Black African patients due to lower baseline renin activity. They work better when combined with a diuretic or calcium channel blocker in this population.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Amlodipine</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Amlodipine works consistently across all ethnic groups and is preferred for initial monotherapy in Black African patients, where RAAS-based drugs are often less effective alone.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Losartan</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>ARBs, like ACE inhibitors, target the RAAS system and are less effective as monotherapy in Black African patients due to lower renin activity.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Atenolol</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Beta-blockers are not a recommended first-line class for uncomplicated hypertension. They are reserved for specific indications such as heart failure or rate control in atrial fibrillation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "In Black African patients, RAAS-based drugs (ACE inhibitors and ARBs) are less effective as monotherapy due to lower renin activity. A calcium channel blocker or thiazide diuretic is preferred as initial treatment."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Calcium channel blockers like amlodipine work independently of the RAAS system and are the preferred first-line monotherapy for Black African patients with hypertension."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
